{"assets":["/editorial-assets/3c20b9f7d19555ca60679adef683bbb990df19711f4a39b01bc86ceb988508ae.png","/editorial-assets/dc86b064c1a09890ed93d4737a872b9ab37ff32f947d26b48124752bad617a82.png","/editorial-assets/2b8d8c140b8d650ef2d62261f1e872463296c34a163d7a21a4b1a372b54197f3.png","/editorial-assets/e1c04d9fb0d6e94da8f529c685cc56a487607b7aa253b6f03d42a1b92a46dd06.png","/editorial-assets/b88eeeaea6cac01bea7b4e2528ffd6efc3e0177015ee623cceeefb3022b3e9e4.png","/editorial-assets/edefd8c06d809196d50a20274f6d1beb3c7b2456fe5d2db2645974a975b8789f.png","/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png","/editorial-assets/b432c23d334e09047956d9416408ed84e7b9667078e9ccc415a7466093cfb2a5.png"],"contestId":"767","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"767A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/767/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"767A - Snacktower"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is enough to do what is written in the statements. You can maintain an array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"has"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and mark in it which snacks has already fallen, and which hasn't. Create another variable "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"next"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" which tracks the next snack which should be put on the top. Let's proceed with the integers in the input one by one. After reading next integer, mark it in the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"has"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" array and go from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"next"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the first snack which is not marked. Print all integers which we passed by."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"767B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/767/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"767B - The Queue"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's calculate the point of time when each visitor would be served. Let array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" contain the points of time when visitors arrive. The receptionist would begin to serve the first visitor at the point of time when the receptionist begins to work "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", if the first visitor came to the passport office before it, or when he comes to the office, if he didn't. We can calculate the point of time when the receptionist would begin to serve the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th visitor in the same way if we know when the receptionist began to serve the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1-th visitor. Let's suppose that the receptionist began to serve the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1-th visitor at "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" minute. It means that receptionist would begin to serve the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th visitor no sooner than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" minutes later, that is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" minute. The receptionist would begin to serve him at this point of time if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th visitor came before ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). If he came later, his serving would begin when he comes. This way we will find the time "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" when the receptionist would begin to serve him."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If any visitor came later than the previous visitor was served ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" > "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), the receptionist was free. It means that Vasya can be served immediately if he arrives at the proper time, for example, at "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" minute. If there are no such visitors, to be the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th person served this day, Vasya has to arrive at the passport office no later than ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1) and he would have to wait a minimum of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1) minutes. From all of these options we have to find a point of time with the minimal waiting time."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are several special cases we have to consider: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-ый and ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1)-ый visitors arrived at the same time, Vasya can't arrive between them. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Some visitors wouldn't be served this day if the time the receptionist would begin to serve them is more or equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and that means we shouldn't attive to the passport office after them. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Vasya can be the last person served this day if there are at least "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" minutes between the point of time receptionist serves the last customer and the point of time he stops working. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Vasya can be the first person served only if he comes before every other visitor. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Considering the 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"12"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" bound, all calculations should use the 64-bit data."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To conclude, this task is reduced to careful calculation of the visitors' serving times ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") time), considering the aforementioned edge cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"767C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/767/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"767C - Garland"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can note that the given graph is a tree. Let's perform a dfs from the root of the tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's calculate the sums if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" in each subtree, let this value be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" for the subtree of the vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". In order to compute "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" we need to recursively call dfs from all sons of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and add the value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let the overall sum of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not divisible by three, there is no answer. Otherwise there are two different cases (let the answer lamps be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") to obtain three subtrees with equal sum ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / 3):"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1. One of the vertices is an ancestor of the other (we can think that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is ancestor of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"), then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / 3, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / 3."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2. Neither "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" nor "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is ancestor of the other. In this case "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / 3"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To check the first option, it is enough to track is the dfs if there is at least one vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the subtree of current vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" with sum "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / 3. If there is one, and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / 3, then there is an answer "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To check the second option, let's write down all vertices "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / 3 and there isno other "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / 3 in the subtree of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Note that we do the same thing when checking the first option. So, if there are at least two vertices we wrote down, they form the answer we are looking for."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"767D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/767/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"767D - Cartons of milk"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the maximum expiry date in the input."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The key observation in this problem is the fact that if we can buy some "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" cartons from the shop and not have to throw away the cartons, we can buy "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" cartons with the biggest expiry dates and we won't have to throw away any cartons either. It happens because if we increase the carton's expiry date while having fixed distribution of cartons per days, the distribution would stay correct."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then, let's learn to check for an arbitrary "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is it true that if we take "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" cartons with the maximum expiry dates we can distribute those cartons per days so that we won't have to throw cartons away. To do this, it is sufficient to check for each day "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from 0 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" that the amount of cartons with expiry dates  ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (both from a fridge and bought) is no bigger than ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1)"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then the solution would be to search for maximum "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" using the binary search. If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the answer, the check would pass for all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from 0 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and wouldn't for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", this monotony is sufficient for the binary search to work. Then we output the found "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" cartons with maximum expiry dates (we don't even have to sort "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", we can justdo an enumeration sort because "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"7"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). This soluton runs in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tlogm"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") time."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"767E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/767/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"767E - Change-free"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first thing to note is that during day "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" it makes sense to either pay "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/3c20b9f7d19555ca60679adef683bbb990df19711f4a39b01bc86ceb988508ae.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" notes и "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/dc86b064c1a09890ed93d4737a872b9ab37ff32f947d26b48124752bad617a82.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" coins (in this case, the cashier's dissatisfaction would be equal to 0), or just "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/2b8d8c140b8d650ef2d62261f1e872463296c34a163d7a21a4b1a372b54197f3.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" notes (in that case, the cashier's dissatisfaction would be equal to "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/e1c04d9fb0d6e94da8f529c685cc56a487607b7aa253b6f03d42a1b92a46dd06.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":")/ Moreover, the second case is impossible if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/b88eeeaea6cac01bea7b4e2528ffd6efc3e0177015ee623cceeefb3022b3e9e4.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", so in that case you just have to pay the required amount of notes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In order to solve the problem, we have to note the additional fact. Let's suppose Arseny paid change-free during the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th day and gave the cashier "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/dc86b064c1a09890ed93d4737a872b9ab37ff32f947d26b48124752bad617a82.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" coins. Then, if we change the payment way this day, the amount of coins availible to Arseny would increase by 100 regardless of the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"! Indeed, Arseny wouldn't spend those "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/dc86b064c1a09890ed93d4737a872b9ab37ff32f947d26b48124752bad617a82.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" coins, and he would aso receive "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/edefd8c06d809196d50a20274f6d1beb3c7b2456fe5d2db2645974a975b8789f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" coins in change, which adds up to exactly 100 coins. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's build the optimal solution day-by-day beginning from day one, trying to pay change-free every time to minimize the cashier's dissatisfaction. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th day be the first one when Arseny wouldn't be able to pay change-free. It means that Arseny has to get some change at least once during days from first to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th. But, regardless of the day, after "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th day he would have the same amount of coins! It means that the optimal way is to get change during the day when the cashier's dissatisfaction would be minimal. Then, let's continue to pay change-free whenever we can. If Arseny again can't pay change-free during day "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", there must be a day from first to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th when he got change. Using similiar considerations, whe should choose the day with the minimal cashier's dissatisfaction (except the first one). We should do these operations until we process all days."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The simple implementation of this process works in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") time and hits TLE. But if you use any structure of data which allows you to add or delete element or find minimum in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" time, for example, heap or binary seach tree, we can save all previous days into it and find a day with the minimal cashier's dissatisfaction faster than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The final time is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/b432c23d334e09047956d9416408ed84e7b9667078e9ccc415a7466093cfb2a5.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/50498"}